 handle progress display for these. For rsync, it already is able to parse rsync output and do a more compact progress display (which --quiet would disable). I don't know if a progress display is doable for wget downloads: git-annex sometimes does not know the final file size, and it would have to inneficiently poll the file as it was downloaded to update the progress, or pipe the download through git-annex to count the bytes.\n\nAnother option would be to /dev/null rsync and wget outout in --quiet mode or have a --no-progress that disables all progress displays. Either would be easy to do.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1413409188,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDU5MjgxMDU5","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/13#issuecomment-59281059"},"message":"that is why I have mentioned #10 happen you decide to approach 'pluggable' downloaders, there should be reserved a mechanism to report progress one way (just to stdout following some convention) or another (accept an option for a file/pipe filename to output progress) based on some way to get it (parsing output) or another (sensing output file knowing target size).  \n\nI guess whenever target size is unknown it is ok to just report some activity progress without explicit % report.\n\nNote: If doing wget output parsing (joey or ourselves) for wget -- there is a `--progress=type` which better get explicitly set to override whatever is provided in ~/.wgetrc.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"fb8c9a505d0037b13268ad0c66d48ae10558561f"},"timestamp":1415826804,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDYyNzk0NDU5","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/13#issuecomment-62794459"},"message":"Maybe consider adding an amount of X parallel get sessions, maybe even split by remotes and/or remote types. This may lead to speedup and allow multi-line progress bars at the same time.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"fb8c9a505d0037b13268ad0c66d48ae10558561f"},"timestamp":1415827060,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDYyNzk1MDgx","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/13#issuecomment-62795081"},"message":"PS: Issue https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/9 is also somewhat related to the above.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1418743376,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDY3MTc1NDAw","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/13#issuecomment-67175400"},"message":"@joeyh \"If there is a way to make wget shut up about http details and still display progress, I'd like to use it.\" -- \"-q --show-progress\" seems to do that, seems to be since 1.16 (according to NEWS):\n\n```\nwget -nc -q --show-progress http://data.pymvpa.org/datasets/tutorial_data/.git//annex/objects/qz/gm/SHA256E-s222--9f67189524fc4e8a114b1860fbad6b248cb9216adfabcea5e96b33dd35566f4c.1D/SHA256E-s222--9f67189524fc4e8a114b1860fbad6b248cb9216adfabcea5e96b33dd35566f4c.1D\nSHA256E-s222--9f67189524fc4e8a114b1860fbad6 100%[==========================================================================================\u003e]     222  --.-KB/s   in 0s\n```\n\nand if you were to jump to parse rsync output, probably wget output could be parsed as well? ;)\ne.g. try\n\n```\nwget -nc -q --show-progress --progress=dot http://data.pymvpa.org/datasets/tutorial_data/tutorial_data-0.2.tar.gz 2\u003e\u00261 | sed -e '/ [0-9][0-9]*%/s,.* \\([0-9][0-9]*%\\) .*,\\1,g'\n```","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1421839958,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDcwODIyNjQ4","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/14#issuecomment-70822648"},"message":"Yes, `--shared` fixes this. I reopened #1 as a result of what came next. Closing this one...","files":null},{"type":4,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":14